Put the problem on the complex plane, so \omega is the unit circle, and let O=0 be the center of \omega. Define \zeta^3=1, \zeta \neq 1. 

Then, B_1, B_2, C_1, C_2 are b\zeta, b\zeta^2, c\zeta, c\zeta^2, respectively. Letting S_1=a+b+c and S_2=bc+ac+ab, we find y=\frac{bS_2}{b^2-ac} \text{ and } z=\frac{cS_2}{c^2-ab} \text{ ,while } \overline{y}=-\frac{S_1}{b^2-ac} \text{ and } \overline{z}=-\frac{S_1}{c^2-ab} P is the center of the spiral similarity sending BC to YZ, so p = \frac{by-cz}{b+y-c-z}=\frac{\frac{b^2S_2}{b^2-ac}-\frac{c^2S_2}{c^2-ab}}{\frac{b^2S_1}{b^2-ac}-\frac{c^2S_1}{c^2-ab}}=\frac{S_2}{S_1}
Claim 1: \overleftrightarrow{YZ} is the perpendicular bisector of \overline{OP}

Proof: To see this, write |y-p|=|y| \iff \overline{p}y+p\overline{y}=1 But, \overline{p}=\frac{1}{p}=\frac{S_1}{S_2}, so \overline{p}y+p\overline{y} = \frac{bS_1-S_2}{b^2-ac} = \frac{b^2-ac}{b^2-ac} = 1 as needed. Similarly, we can show |z-p|=|z|, proving our claim.

Now, we move onto D. Let K=\frac{1}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)}. With lots of help from factoring, we derive D=  \frac{(\overline{y}z-y\overline{z})(b-c) + (y-z)(\frac{c}{b}-\frac{b}{c})}{(\overline{y}-\overline{z})(b-c)+(y-z)(\frac{1}{b}-\frac{1}{c})} =\frac{(\overline{y}z-y\overline{z})bc + (y-z)(b+c)}{(\overline{y}-\overline{z})bc+(y-z)} = \frac{bcS_1S_2(b-c)K+(b+c)S_2S_2(c-b)K}{bcS_1S_1(b-c)K+S_2S_2(c-b)K}=\frac{(b+c)S_2^2-bcS_1S_2}{S_2^2-bcS_1^2} Similarly, E=\frac{(a+p)S_2^2-apS_1S_2}{S_2^2-apS_1^2}=\frac{pS_2}{S_2-aS_1} where we have used p=\frac{S_2}{S_1}. To finish, we write |D|=|E|\iff \left| \frac{S_2(S_2(b+c)-S_1)}{S_2^2-bcS_1^2} \right|=\left| \frac{S_2}{bc-a^2}\right| \iff \left| \frac{(bc-a^2)(b^2+bc+c^2)}{S_2^2-bcS_1^2}\right| = 1 \quad \quad (\ast)  where we have used S_2(b+c)-S_1bc=a(b^2+bc+c^2). But, S_2^2-bcS_1^2 = a^2b^2+a^2bc+ac^2-b^3c-b^2c^2-bc^3 = (a^2-bc)(b^2+bc+c^2) Thus, the fraction in (\ast) is -1, and so we conclude |D|=|E|. Thus, PD=OD=OE=PE \quad \square

